</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Effect of Trend-aware Inference</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A4.T13" title="Table 13 ‣ D.1 Effect of Inference Timestamp Shift ‣ Appendix D Additional Case Study ‣ Enhancing Time Awareness in Generative Recommendation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> illustrates how GRUT benefits from the trend score <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\text{trend}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mtext>trend</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\text{trend}}</annotation></semantics></math> to better capture user preference. The user had recently purchased the ‘<span id="A4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">LEGO Sorting Systems</span>’, so various toy-related products appear as top recommendations when <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> = 0 in Eq. (<a href="#S4.E10" title="In 4.3 Trend-aware Inference ‣ 4 Proposed Model ‣ Enhancing Time Awareness in Generative Recommendation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>). Considering temporal trends during inference, the ranking of trending items
‘<span id="A4.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Rainbow Loom</span>’ was elevated, resulting in recommendations that closely aligned with the user preferences. This demonstrates that Trend-aware Inference enables the model to combine time-sensitive trends with the user’s intrinsic preference, producing more accurate and timely recommendations. Furthermore, the ability to control the influence of the <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\text{trend}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mtext>trend</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\text{trend}}</annotation></semantics></math> based on user needs highlights the practical advantage of the proposed method in terms of <span id="A4.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">controllability</span>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
